window.QUEST = {"six":["sort","straighten","shine","safety","standardize","sustain"],"colours":{"sort":"#CB4B36","straighten":"#BC4B2A","shine":"#D98A2B","safety":"#DDA63A","standardize":"#6E8B5B","sustain":"#4E7A57"},"purpose":{"sort":"Decide what stays. Nothing else.","straighten":"Give what stayed a home you can reach.","shine":"Clean it, and see what the cleaning tells you.","safety":"Fix what could hurt somebody. The fourth S, not the last.","standardize":"Write down what good looks like, so it is not a memory.","sustain":"Attach the reset to something that already happens."},"symptoms":[{"symptom":"Keys, chargers and sunglasses land beside the tray, not in it","room":"Entryway","zone":"Landing Zone","why":"The tray is not where my hand actually opens on the way in","sixS":"Straighten","action":"Empty the tray and the paper stack onto the surface, then give every sheet a verdict: act, file, or recycle, before anything goes back.","victory":"One tray holds only keys and sunglasses, and no loose paper sits anywhere on the surface.","img":"entryway--landing-zone","url":"/zones/entryway-the-landing-spot"},{"symptom":"The rail is full and there is still no empty hook","room":"Entryway","zone":"Coat and Outerwear Zone","why":"There is a coat for a weather category that already has one","sixS":"Sort","action":"Take down every coat that did not go outside once this cold season, and clear the two hooks nearest the door.","victory":"Two hooks stand empty nearest the door, and every coat still on the rail was worn this season.","img":"entryway--coat-and-outerwear-zone","url":"/zones/entryway-the-coats-and-outerwear"},{"symptom":"The counter is never clear","room":"Kitchen","zone":"Primary Prep Counter","why":"Things get set down here on the way past","sixS":"Straighten","action":"Get one unbroken run of counter back, and prove it can hold.","victory":"Your largest cutting board lies flat with room on both sides, and nothing else is on the run.","img":"kitchen--primary-prep-counter","url":"/zones/kitchen-the-primary-prep-counter"},{"symptom":"The junk drawer takes anything","room":"Kitchen","zone":"Utensil and Utility Drawers","why":"The things in it have no home anywhere else","sixS":"Straighten","action":"One drawer, one job, and it closes with one push.","victory":"You can name each drawer's job, and each one closes with one push.","img":"kitchen--utensil-and-utility-drawers","url":"/zones/kitchen-the-utensil-and-utility-drawers"},{"symptom":"The sink is full again by evening","room":"Kitchen","zone":"Sink and Dishwashing Zone","why":"There is no moment in the day when it gets cleared","sixS":"Sustain","action":"Empty basin, dry basin, two tools standing.","victory":"Dry basin, two tools standing, nothing lying in water.","img":"kitchen--sink-and-dishwashing-zone","url":"/zones/kitchen-the-sink-and-dishwashing-zone"},{"symptom":"The counter is covered again two days after I clear it","room":"Primary Bathroom","zone":"Vanity Counter","why":"The things on it are ones we use every single day","sixS":"Sort","action":"Take everything off the counter, wipe the bare stone and the mirror, then put back only the soap, the toothbrush holder and the four products you touched today.","victory":"Bare stone on both sides of the basin, and one tray you can lift with one hand.","img":"primary-bathroom--vanity-counter","url":"/zones/primary-bathroom-the-vanity-counter"},{"symptom":"Pulling one towel out brings the stack down, or I need a stool to reach it","room":"Primary Bathroom","zone":"Linen and Towel Storage","why":"The everyday towels are on a shelf above comfortable reach","sixS":"Safety","action":"Take the shelf down to three bath towels per person, nest each guest set in its own pillowcase, and put hand towels and washcloths into separate labeled columns.","victory":"Three bath towels per person on the shelf, and every guest set in its own pillowcase.","img":"primary-bathroom--linen-and-towel-storage","url":"/zones/primary-bathroom-the-linen-and-towel-storage"},{"symptom":"I clear the desk and it is covered again by the end of the week","room":"Home Office","zone":"Primary Desk","why":"Paper lands here because there is nowhere else to put it","sixS":"Straighten","action":"Take everything off the desk except the monitor, keyboard and mouse. Put the loose paper into the inbox tray, give every sheet in it a verdict until it is under a dozen, and hook the power strip up off the floor.","victory":"One notebook and one tray under a dozen sheets, and the chair rolls the width of the desk without catching.","img":"home-office--primary-desk","url":"/zones/home-office-the-primary-desk"},{"symptom":"I run out of paper or ink mid-job","room":"Home Office","zone":"Printer and Scanning Station","why":"There is no min line, so nobody sees low coming","sixS":"Standardize","action":"Clear the top of and the space behind the printer, draw a min line and a max line on the paper bin, and split the scan tray into a to-do side and a done side.","victory":"Air behind the machine, a paper level anyone can read at a glance, and a scan tray that says what still needs doing.","img":null,"url":"/zones/home-office-the-printer-and-scanning-station"},{"symptom":"The bench is never clear enough to start a job on","room":"Garage","zone":"Primary Workbench","why":"Finished jobs are pushed aside rather than put away","sixS":"Sustain","action":"Clear the bench top down to the vise and the task light, put the current job in one tray, rack the clamps on the rail, and sweep until you can see concrete under the bench.","victory":"A bare bench, one tray holding one job, and swept concrete visible underneath.","img":"garage--primary-workbench","url":"/zones/garage-the-primary-workbench"},{"symptom":"Long-handled tools live leaning in a corner","room":"Garage","zone":"Lawn and Garden Tool Zone","why":"There are more handles than there are hooks on the rail","sixS":"Sort","action":"Hang every long handle head-up on the rail, coil the hose onto its reel beside the door it goes out of, and move every garden chemical into a latched cupboard above head height, binning anything whose label you cannot read.","victory":"Nothing leaning in a corner, a hose on its reel by the right door, and every chemical labeled, latched and above head height.","img":"garage--lawn-and-garden-tool-zone","url":"/zones/garage-the-lawn-and-garden-tool-zone"},{"symptom":"Washing sits in the drum long enough to smell, and gets rewashed","room":"Laundry Room","zone":"Washer and Dryer","why":"Nothing marks the moment a cycle ends","sixS":"Sustain","action":"Empty both drums, take everything off both lids, clear the lint screen and put it back, prop the washer door ajar, and write this month on a strip of tape on the side of the dryer.","victory":"Both drums empty, both lids bare, the door propped open, and a date on the dryer you can read from the doorway.","img":"laundry-room--washer-and-dryer","url":"/zones/laundry-room-the-washer-and-dryer"},{"symptom":"The rack is permanently up and permanently loaded","room":"Laundry Room","zone":"Hanging and Air-Dry Zone","why":"Things stay on it after they are dry because nothing prompts a check","sixS":"Sustain","action":"Take everything off the rack that was washed before today, put the dry things away, wipe out the drip tray, fold the rack flat against the wall, and put six spare hangers on the rail.","victory":"The rack folded flat with dry bars, an empty tray beneath it, and nothing hanging that was not washed today.","img":"laundry-room--hanging-and-air-dry-zone","url":"/zones/laundry-room-the-hanging-and-air-dry-zone"},{"symptom":"Someone has to move a pile of folded laundry, a stray magazine, or a third throw blanket before they can sit down on the sofa","room":"Living Room","zone":"Sofa and Seating Zone","why":"The laundry doesn't have anywhere else to land on its way through the house, so the sofa catches it","sixS":"Straighten","action":"Pull everything off the seats and dig the seams out: the laundry that migrated here, the second and third throw blanket, the magazines wedged behind the armrest, the coins and hair ties down the back. Sort into leaves-the-room, goes-in-the-wash, and lives-here.","victory":"Every seat is sittable without moving anything, and the throws are folded in one basket.","img":"living-room--sofa-and-seating-zone","url":"/zones/living-room-the-sofa-and-seating"},{"symptom":"A box that arrived weeks ago is still sitting beside the sofa, along with today's shoes and yesterday's school bag","room":"Living Room","zone":"Floor and Circulation Path","why":"Nothing on this floor has anywhere else assigned to go, so it just stays where it landed","sixS":"Straighten","action":"Walk the route with a laundry basket and put every floor item in it: shoes, toys, yesterday's bag, the pile of post, the box that has sat beside the sofa for a month. Anything belonging to another room gets carried there before you let yourself sit down.","victory":"The route from door to door is clear at full width, with nothing on the floor but furniture legs and the rug.","img":"living-room--floor-and-circulation-path","url":"/zones/living-room-the-floor-and-circulation-path"},{"symptom":"A drawer needs a shove or a press-down to close, and it is the one holding workout tops or t-shirts","room":"Primary Bedroom","zone":"Dresser Drawers","why":"You own more of that category than you actually wear, six workout tops when you wear two","sixS":"Sort","action":"Open the drawer that needs a shove to close and pull one full category's worth of overflow out right now: extra workout tops, a wrong-size stack, or loose mothballs, whichever is worst.","victory":"Every drawer closes without being pressed down, and a hand's width of free space shows in each one.","img":"primary-bedroom--dresser-drawers","url":"/zones/primary-bedroom-the-dresser-drawers"},{"symptom":"There is medication, capped or not, sitting loose in the open drawer on this side","room":"Primary Bedroom","zone":"Nightstand Right","why":"It is a poisoning risk at exactly the height a toddler or a dog reaches from the mattress, and that is worth raising even though the rest of the drawer is not yours to touch","sixS":"Safety","action":"Check the medication dates together right now: cap anything loose, and if a child or a dog gets onto this bed, move it into a closed box. Then run the lamp cord behind the leg on this side to match the other.","victory":"Medication on this side is capped and closed away, and the lamp cord runs behind the leg instead of across the floor.","img":"primary-bedroom--nightstand-right","url":"/zones/primary-bedroom-the-other-sleeper-s-nightstand"},{"symptom":"Homework, mail, or a craft project has been sitting on the table for days, migrating a few inches each evening but never actually leaving","room":"Dining Room","zone":"Dining Table","why":"That activity doesn't have anywhere else in the house to happen","sixS":"Straighten","action":"Clear the whole table onto the floor in one armful, then sort what came off by owner rather than by type. The homework, the unopened mail, and the half-finished craft project each go back to a person, not back to the table.","victory":"The table holds nothing but its centerpiece, and every activity that was on it has gone home with the person who owns it.","img":"dining-room--dining-table","url":"/zones/dining-room-the-dining-table"},{"symptom":"A bottle of wine and a couple of spirits sit open on a shelf at this station, within easy reach of a small child standing at the counter","room":"Dining Room","zone":"Beverage or Coffee Station","why":"There's no latch or high shelf assigned for alcohol at this station, only in the kitchen","sixS":"Straighten","action":"Line up every tea box, syrup bottle, and pod sleeve and check the dates, then open the travel mugs and match them to their lids. Anything past date, any mug missing its lid, and the promotional glassware you have never once poured into are out.","victory":"Everything on the counter is in date, every travel mug has its matching lid, and no glassware sits here unused.","img":"dining-room--beverage-or-coffee-station","url":"/zones/dining-room-the-beverage-or-coffee-station"},{"symptom":"A bottle of bleach sits on the same shelf as an ammonia-based glass cleaner, both within reach from the hallway floor","room":"Hall Closet","zone":"Cleaning Supply Zone","why":"Nobody sorted this shelf by what's safe to store together, only by what fits","sixS":"Safety","action":"Line every bottle up on the hallway floor. Anything decanted into an unmarked spray bottle gets disposed of according to its own instructions, and the specialty cleaner bought for one stain years ago goes with it. Only identical products get poured together.","victory":"Every bottle on the shelf is in its own original, labeled container, and no two different products have been mixed.","img":"hall-closet--cleaning-supply-zone","url":"/zones/hall-closet-the-cleaning-supply-zone"},{"symptom":"A warehouse pack of paper towels bought on a deal is too big to fit in its bin, so it sits blocking the shelf instead","room":"Hall Closet","zone":"Paper and Household Backstock","why":"There was no written maximum before the deal, so nothing stopped you buying it","sixS":"Standardize","action":"Take the lot out. Loose batteries you cannot vouch for, bulbs for fittings you replaced when you went over to LED, and the bulk paper towel pack too big to lift down alone all leave now.","victory":"Every battery is in its original pack, every bulb fits a fitting the house still uses, and nothing on the shelf is too heavy to lift down alone.","img":"hall-closet--paper-and-household-backstock","url":"/zones/hall-closet-the-paper-and-household-backstock"},{"symptom":"A can with a dented seam or a jar with a popped lid is still sitting on the shelf instead of already in the bin","room":"Pantry","zone":"Canned and Jarred Goods","why":"I wasn't sure whether a small dent or a slightly domed lid really counts as spoiled","sixS":"Standardize","action":"Take every can and jar off the shelf, turn each one to find the date, and put anything dented, rusted, bulging or domed straight into the bin rather than back on the shelf.","victory":"No dented, rusted, domed or bulging can or jar remains on the shelf, and every label faces out.","img":"pantry--canned-and-jarred-goods","url":"/zones/pantry-the-canned-and-jarred-goods"},{"symptom":"The open snack bin sits below the marked fill line most mornings, well before the week is over","room":"Pantry","zone":"Snack and Lunch Zone","why":"Nobody actually refills it to the line the evening before, it just gets remembered some nights and not others","sixS":"Sustain","action":"Match every lid to a container and bin the orphans in both directions, the lidless tubs and the lids for tubs that died. Pull any snack boxes with only a couple of bars rattling around and combine them.","victory":"Every reusable container has its own lid sitting on it, and the open bin is filled to its marked line.","img":"pantry--snack-and-lunch-zone","url":"/zones/pantry-the-snack-and-lunch-zone"},{"symptom":"A game box has been missing one piece for longer than anyone can remember, and it never got a sticky note or a deadline","room":"Family Room","zone":"Board Game and Puzzle Zone","why":"The missing piece is structural, a board section or a single puzzle piece, and the game is already over even though the box still looks fine on the shelf","sixS":"Sort","action":"Pull every box and check its lid for a name label and a tape strip on the short edge. While each one is open, count the pieces against the box's own list. If something is missing, decide now whether it's substitutable (a token, a die, a bill of play money you can replace) or structural (a rules booklet, a board section, a single puzzle piece). Write the missing item and today's date on a sticky note on any box you are not fixing immediately.","victory":"Every box on the shelf is labeled and stacked no more than five high, and any box missing a piece carries a dated sticky note naming exactly what is gone.","img":"family-room--board-game-and-puzzle-zone","url":"/zones/family-room-the-board-game-and-puzzle-zone"},{"symptom":"A fleece throw is draped over the radiator to dry or just to be out of the way, right where the room's heat source runs hottest","room":"Family Room","zone":"Blanket and Comfort Zone","why":"Synthetic fabric left against a hot surface once the room empties is a real fire risk, and that overrides how convenient the spot is","sixS":"Safety","action":"Pull every throw and cushion out and fold each throw to the same rectangle so the fold edges line up in the basket. Run the reaches test out loud: which ones actually get pulled off the pile in an average week. The decorative one nobody reaches for goes to the guest bed or out, and a genuine heirloom nobody unfolds goes to the linen closet or to the person who will actually use it.","victory":"One basket holds one throw per regular seat plus one spare, all folded to the same rectangle, and nothing is draped over the sofa back, a radiator, or a chair arm.","img":"family-room--blanket-and-comfort-zone","url":"/zones/family-room-the-blanket-and-comfort-zone"},{"symptom":"A box on this shelf has been sealed since a previous address, and nobody can say what's inside without opening it","room":"Guest Bedroom","zone":"Guest Closet","why":"Opening it feels like it could cost an afternoon, so it keeps getting put off","sixS":"Sort","action":"Take everything out and put it on the bed. This closet is where the house keeps holiday decorations, a wedding dress in a zipped bag, a box of old phones, and paperwork from two addresses ago. Sort by whether a named person will use it in a named situation, and route the rest out.","victory":"At least a forearm's width of clear rod carries six matching empty hangers, and the floor square for a suitcase is clear.","img":"guest-bedroom--guest-closet","url":"/zones/guest-bedroom-the-guest-closet"},{"symptom":"A bag of outgrown baby clothes is still in this dresser, kept for a second child nobody has actually decided about","room":"Guest Bedroom","zone":"Guest Dresser","why":"It's not clutter, it's a decision about whether we're having another child that I haven't made yet","sixS":"Sort","action":"This is where the household's undecided things hide behind a closed front: off-season sweaters, a bin of cables, wrapping paper and ribbon, a bag of outgrown baby clothes waiting on a decision about a second child. The sweaters go to your own wardrobe, the cables to the drawer that already holds cables, and the baby clothes get the decision today rather than another year of storage.","victory":"The top two drawers stand empty and lined, and the lower drawers hold only spare linens for this room's bed.","img":"guest-bedroom--guest-dresser","url":"/zones/guest-bedroom-the-guest-dresser"},{"symptom":"A blind cord or looped drawstring hangs down near the pillow, well within reach of a sleeping child's neck","room":"Kids Bedroom","zone":"Bed and Sleep Zone","why":"A cord or loop hanging at a sleeping child's neck height is a strangling risk that outranks how the window dressing looks","sixS":"Safety","action":"Check every blind or curtain cord near the bed head right now and cleat any hanging loop up out of a sleeping child's reach. Strip the duvet and pillow off, count how many stuffed animals were actually in the bed, and move the rest into the basket at the foot where they're still visible. Square the pillow and pull the duvet flat before you finish.","victory":"No cord or loop hangs within reach of the pillow, the bed carries a squared pillow and a flat duvet with only the animals that fit in two arms on top, and the rest sit visible in the basket at the foot.","img":"kids-bedroom--bed-and-sleep-zone","url":"/zones/kids-bedroom-the-bed-and-sleep-zone"},{"symptom":"A drawer needs a hard yank to open because it's overstuffed, and it comes free suddenly enough to pull the child backwards off balance","room":"Kids Bedroom","zone":"Dresser Drawers","why":"A jammed drawer that gives suddenly when it finally opens is a fall risk that outranks how full the drawer looks","sixS":"Safety","action":"Open every drawer right now and push on it once without leaning. Any drawer that needs a press to close gets emptied onto the bed immediately, and anything with dead elastic, no pair, or a hem that now stops above the ankle comes out for good. Refile what's left standing upright before you move to the next drawer.","victory":"Every drawer closes with a single push, socks and underwear stand upright rather than lying flat, and nothing with a broken pair, dead elastic or the wrong size is back in a drawer.","img":"kids-bedroom--dresser-drawers","url":"/zones/kids-bedroom-the-dresser-drawers"},{"symptom":"There's an outfit in the drawer with the tags still on, in a size your baby has already outgrown","room":"Nursery","zone":"Baby Clothing Zone","why":"It was a gift from someone who mattered, and letting it go feels like a small betrayal","sixS":"Sort","action":"Open every drawer, pull anything smaller than what your baby is wearing today, and put it straight into the outgoing bag on the door hook.","victory":"Every drawer holds one size only, and the outgoing bag on the door has something in it.","img":"nursery--baby-clothing-zone","url":"/zones/nursery-the-baby-clothing-zone"},{"symptom":"A paper-page book or one of your own books is sitting on the low ledge within the baby's reach","room":"Nursery","zone":"Books and Quiet Play Zone","why":"It was chosen because you wanted to read it aloud, and moving it off the ledge can feel like giving up that plan","sixS":"Sort","action":"Move every paper-page book off the low ledge to a shelf in your own room, and swap the soft toy basket down to level with its rim, boxing the rest for the closet rotation.","victory":"The low ledge holds only board books facing out, and the soft toy basket sits level with its rim, not above it.","img":"nursery--books-and-quiet-play-zone","url":"/zones/nursery-the-books-and-quiet-play-zone"},{"symptom":"The reserve roll is mounted low on the wall, and a seated guest has to stand up to reach it","room":"Guest Bathroom","zone":"Toilet Area","why":"It went into whatever holder was already installed, never tested with someone actually seated","sixS":"Safety","action":"Clear everything from the top of the tank and the floor behind the bowl: the collection of air fresheners, the second brush, the magazines, the box of something nobody has identified in years. One reserve roll stays in the open. Nothing else.","victory":"The tank top and the floor behind the bowl are bare except for one reserve roll standing in the open.","img":"guest-bathroom--toilet-area","url":"/zones/guest-bathroom-the-toilet-area"},{"symptom":"A cup on this counter is holding a toothbrush that clearly belongs to someone who lives here, not a visitor","room":"Guest Bathroom","zone":"Guest Vanity Counter","why":"Someone in this house genuinely brushes their teeth in here every day, and nobody's said that out loud yet","sixS":"Standardize","action":"Take everything off the counter and put back only what a visitor would use: soap, tissues, hand towel. The travel conditioner, the spare contact lens case, and the razor that ended up here because the main bathroom ran out of room all go back where they belong or into the trash.","victory":"Only soap, tissues and a folded hand towel remain on the counter, with bare space enough for a phone and glasses, and nothing of the household's left behind.","img":"guest-bathroom--guest-vanity-counter","url":"/zones/guest-bathroom-the-guest-vanity-counter"},{"symptom":"A blade guard does not spring back on its own anymore when you release it","room":"Workshop","zone":"Power Tool Storage","why":"A guard that sticks is the injury this zone is actually waiting on, and that outranks how small a fix it seems","sixS":"Safety","action":"Work the retracting guard on every saw with your thumb to confirm it snaps back on its own, and move any battery still sitting on the charger from a finished job onto its tool's hook.","victory":"Every guard snaps shut on its own, and no charger is running behind a job that already ended.","img":"workshop--power-tool-storage","url":"/zones/workshop-the-power-tool-storage"},{"symptom":"The extinguisher gauge is not sitting in the green, or there is no inspection date on the bracket tape","room":"Workshop","zone":"Safety and PPE Station","why":"A dead extinguisher looks identical to a working one until the moment you need it, and that outranks how rarely you check the gauge","sixS":"Safety","action":"Lift the extinguisher and confirm the gauge sits in the green, then run a hand over every pair of glasses on the hooks and bin any pair scratched enough that you would lift them off to see a cut line.","victory":"The extinguisher gauge reads green with a dated tape on the bracket, and every pair of glasses left on the hooks is clear enough to cut by.","img":"workshop--safety-and-ppe-station","url":"/zones/workshop-the-safety-and-ppe-station"},{"symptom":"The old vacuum has held its corner for over a year, but the main one has never actually broken down long enough to need it","room":"Mudroom","zone":"Cleaning and Utility Zone","why":"Getting rid of a machine that still works feels wasteful, even though it isn't functioning as an actual backup","sixS":"Sort","action":"Shake the door mats out right now, hang the broom back on its clip with the bristles clear of the floor, and check whether the mop head has actually dried. Pull the decanted, unlabeled bottle out of the caddy and label it, or empty it if you can't tell what it is.","victory":"The broom, mop and dustpan all hang clear of the floor, the mop head is dry, and every bottle in the caddy is labeled.","img":"mudroom--cleaning-and-utility-zone","url":"/zones/mudroom-the-cleaning-and-utility-zone"},{"symptom":"The bag of unmatched single gloves has survived three changeovers already, including a good ski glove nobody will actually throw out","room":"Mudroom","zone":"Seasonal Outdoor Gear","why":"The glove is expensive, and letting it go without finding its pair feels wasteful even three seasons on","sixS":"Sort","action":"Tip every glove, mitten and hat from this season's bin onto the floor and match them into pairs. Put any single into the dated singles bag, and check the sunscreen and insect repellent for their dates, moving anything expired out of the low bin.","victory":"Every glove and mitten in the bin is matched into a pair, the singles bag carries today's date, and no expired sunscreen or insect repellent remains in the low bin.","img":"mudroom--seasonal-outdoor-gear","url":"/zones/mudroom-the-seasonal-outdoor-gear"},{"symptom":"Things ride the stair basket for days without ever landing where they actually belong","room":"Stair Landing","zone":"Landing Surface or Console","why":"Nothing marks the moment to carry it, so it waits for a trip that never comes on its own","sixS":"Sustain","action":"Clear the console top and drawer in one sweep: keep only what truly lives on this floor, drop anything headed to another floor straight into the stair basket, and bag up the loose screws, dead pens and read mail that have drifted in.","victory":"The console top holds only its permanent items and an empty tray, and the stair basket on the floor is empty.","img":"stair-landing--landing-surface-or-console","url":"/zones/stair-landing-the-landing-surface-or-console"},{"symptom":"A lifted runner corner or a loose rod gets pressed back into place and left instead of actually refixed","room":"Stair Landing","zone":"Stair and Floor Path","why":"Fixing it properly means clearing the whole flight and buying rods or tape, and that's a bigger job than the few minutes I have when I notice it","sixS":"Sort","action":"Clear every tread of anything sitting on it, laundry, shoes, a box, in one trip to where it actually belongs, then stand at the bottom of the flight and check that both the top and bottom lights actually come on.","victory":"Every tread is bare from nose to riser, and both the top and bottom stair lights work.","img":"stair-landing--stair-and-floor-path","url":"/zones/stair-landing-the-stair-and-floor-path"},{"symptom":"A saucer under a pot is holding standing water days after the last rain, or the upturned wheelbarrow has a puddle sitting in its well","room":"Patio or Deck","zone":"Garden and Plant Care Zone","why":"Checking every saucer only takes ten seconds, but nothing about filling the watering can actually forces you to look down at them first","sixS":"Sustain","action":"Walk the row of saucers, the wheelbarrow well, and any upturned pot lid tipping out standing water, then pull any pot with no drainage hole or last year's dead root ball out of the nested stack.","victory":"No saucer, wheelbarrow well, or pot lid on the patio holds standing water, and every pot in the nested stack has a clear drain hole and nothing dead in it.","img":"patio-or-deck--garden-and-plant-care-zone","url":"/zones/patio-or-deck-the-garden-and-plant-care-zone"},{"symptom":"A planter has drifted into the path between the door and the steps, a hose is coiled across the top step, or a bag of paving sand leans against a rail post","room":"Patio or Deck","zone":"Surface, Rail, and Safety Zone","why":"None of it looks like it is blocking anything until you are actually carrying something with both arms and cannot see your feet","sixS":"Sort","action":"Walk the full route from the door to the steps to the gate carrying a full laundry basket in both arms, and pull off the route anything you have to step around.","victory":"The full route from the door to the steps to the gate is clear enough to walk carrying a full laundry basket without stepping around anything.","img":"patio-or-deck--surface-rail-and-safety-zone","url":"/zones/patio-or-deck-the-surface-rail-and-safety-zone"},{"symptom":"This area smells even after cleaning it","room":"Primary Bathroom","zone":"Toilet Area","why":"The brush goes back into its holder wet","sixS":"Standardize","action":"Clear the cistern lid completely, empty and dry the brush holder, put a liner and a lid on the bin, and set two reserve rolls within reach from the seat.","victory":"A completely bare cistern lid, and two reserve rolls reachable without standing up.","img":"primary-bathroom--toilet-area","url":"/zones/primary-bathroom-the-toilet-area"},{"symptom":"The unit rocks or leans when I pull a book out","room":"Home Office","zone":"Bookshelf and Reference Zone","why":"It is not fixed to the wall, and it stands on carpet or an uneven floor","sixS":"Safety","action":"Move every heavy binder to the bottom two shelves, bring the reference you actually open to seated eye level, then check the wall fixing and fit one if it is missing.","victory":"The heaviest things are lowest, the unit does not move when you pull a book, and every row ends in a hand's width of space.","img":"home-office--bookshelf-and-reference-zone","url":"/zones/home-office-the-bookshelf-and-reference-zone"},{"symptom":"Something here is a fire or poisoning risk","room":"Garage","zone":"Automotive Care Zone","why":"Oily rags are in an open or plastic bin","sixS":"Safety","action":"Stand every bottle upright on one wipeable tray, write today's date on the shoulder of each one you have opened, bin anything that fits no car on this driveway, and put the oily rags in a metal can with a lid.","victory":"Every bottle upright and dated on one tray, nothing for a car you do not own, and the rags in a closed metal can.","img":"garage--automotive-care-zone","url":"/zones/garage-the-automotive-care-zone"},{"symptom":"There is something down here a child could open","room":"Laundry Room","zone":"Detergent and Treatment Zone","why":"The pod tub sits at or below a child's eye level","sixS":"Safety","action":"Bring every laundry product onto one wipeable tray. Keep one working bottle of each kind, ink the true dose line on each cap, and latch the pod tub above shoulder height.","victory":"One of each kind standing on a wipeable tray, a dose line you can see on every cap, and nothing a child can reach.","img":"laundry-room--detergent-and-treatment-zone","url":"/zones/laundry-room-the-detergent-and-treatment-zone"},{"symptom":"Loose tablets sit in an open dish on this table, right at the height a small child standing beside the chair would reach","room":"Living Room","zone":"Side Tables and Lighting","why":"There's no rule that medicine goes in a lidded case instead of an open dish","sixS":"Safety","action":"Empty the little dish and the drawer onto the seat of the chair. The reading glasses with the wrong prescription, the dried-out pens, the foreign coins, the loose tablets, the charger for a phone nobody in the house owns and the coasters that never made it back to the coffee table each get a verdict now.","victory":"Each table's tray holds at most four items, and nothing swallowable sits uncapped.","img":"living-room--side-tables-and-lighting","url":"/zones/living-room-the-side-tables-and-lighting"},{"symptom":"There is an open glass of water sitting on the same small top as the lamp and a power strip","room":"Primary Bedroom","zone":"Nightstand Left","why":"It is a single knocked elbow from water and electricity meeting, and that outranks the convenience of a lidless glass","sixS":"Safety","action":"Empty the top down to five items and empty the drawer onto the bed: the dead pen, the chargers for phones you do not own, and any book you have not picked up this week go straight to the shelf or the bin.","victory":"The nightstand top holds five things or fewer with no cable crossing it, and the drawer holds only what you would actually reach for tonight.","img":"primary-bedroom--nightstand-left","url":"/zones/primary-bedroom-your-own-nightstand"},{"symptom":"The top of this cabinet, high and out of easy sight, has a visible layer of dust nobody's touched in a long time","room":"Dining Room","zone":"China or Display Cabinet","why":"Reaching up there means finding a stool first, so it's the last thing anyone bothers with","sixS":"Shine","action":"Take every piece out and split it into three groups: complete sets, chipped or crazed pieces, and lone survivors of sets that are long gone. A chipped rim cannot be mended and is not safe to drink from, so that whole group leaves together.","victory":"What's left behind the glass is complete sets and pieces without a chip or crack, nothing kept only out of habit.","img":"dining-room--china-or-display-cabinet","url":"/zones/dining-room-the-china-or-display-cabinet"},{"symptom":"A broom handle has slid down the wall again and is lying across the doorway instead of hanging from its clip","room":"Hall Closet","zone":"Cleaning Equipment Zone","why":"The clip is the wrong size for this handle so it never really holds","sixS":"Sort","action":"Stand every handle up and look at the working end. Brooms with splayed bristles that push dust rather than gather it, the mop head that no longer twists off its plate, and the old vacuum you keep for parts you have never once harvested all go out this week.","victory":"Every remaining tool has a working end, and nothing is being kept for parts that were never actually used.","img":"hall-closet--cleaning-equipment-zone","url":"/zones/hall-closet-the-cleaning-equipment-zone"},{"symptom":"The nut flour or sesame container shares a scoop with everything else on this shelf","room":"Pantry","zone":"Baking Zone","why":"Nobody ever agreed this container needs its own dedicated scoop","sixS":"Standardize","action":"Test every leavener rather than guessing: a spoon of baking powder in hot water should fizz hard, and yeast in warm sugared water should foam. The dead ones go, along with any hardened brown sugar or grayed cocoa.","victory":"Every leavener in the bin has been tested this week, and nothing dead or expired remains.","img":"pantry--baking-zone","url":"/zones/pantry-the-baking-zone"},{"symptom":"A tablet is charging under a blanket on the sofa cushion instead of on the strip, and it's warm to the touch","room":"Family Room","zone":"Charging and Device Zone","why":"Charging on soft material that traps heat against a battery is a fire risk that overrides where it's convenient to leave it","sixS":"Safety","action":"Match every cable at the station to a device the house actually uses, and keep one spare of each connector type in a labeled bag. Pull the retired phone out of the drawer, charge it, and decide out loud whether it is genuinely a backup or an archive. If it is an archive, transfer the photos now while it is charged and in your hand; if it is neither, recycle it with the battery still in it at a proper collection point.","victory":"Every cable at the station ends at a named device the house uses, the retired phone has been settled as backup, archive, or recycled, and no charger is plugged in anywhere else in the room.","img":"family-room--charging-and-device-zone","url":"/zones/family-room-the-charging-and-device-zone"},{"symptom":"Something that is not a suitcase is sitting under the guest bed when you finally look","room":"Guest Bedroom","zone":"Guest Bed and Linens","why":"It was easier to set it down here than decide where it actually belongs","sixS":"Sort","action":"Take every sheet set that has been demoted to this room and try each fitted sheet on the actual mattress. If a corner pops off while you are making the bed, it is a rag, not a spare. Fold each pillow in half and let go, and anything that stays folded goes out.","victory":"Every remaining sheet set has passed the mattress test, and every remaining pillow springs back when folded in half.","img":"guest-bedroom--guest-bed-and-linens","url":"/zones/guest-bedroom-the-guest-bed-and-linens"},{"symptom":"A lamp, a laptop charger and a second extension strip are all chained into one strip under the desk, with the water bottle sitting at the same end","room":"Kids Bedroom","zone":"Study Desk","why":"A chain of strips feeding a desk this size is an overloaded socket, a safety constraint that outranks how convenient the chain was to build","sixS":"Safety","action":"Clear the desk down to bare wood right now. Sort every loose sheet of paper into exactly one of three piles, live work into the tray, keepsake into the memory box, everything else into recycling, and count the plugs under the desk, bringing any chain of strips back to one strip in one wall socket.","victory":"The desk holds only the lamp, the pen cup and one tray of live work, every other sheet of paper has a verdict, and exactly one power strip runs from exactly one wall socket.","img":"kids-bedroom--study-desk","url":"/zones/kids-bedroom-the-study-desk"},{"symptom":"A heavy carton or pack is stored on a shelf above or beside the crib","room":"Nursery","zone":"Diaper and Care Backstock","why":"Weight that can shift and fall into the sleep space outranks whatever convenience put it there","sixS":"Safety","action":"Pull every pack off the shelf, read the printed size, and take anything smaller than today's size, opened or not, off the shelf. Move anything heavy off any shelf above or beside the crib.","victory":"The shelf holds one unopened pack of the current size, no more than two packs of the next size, and nothing heavy sits above or beside the crib.","img":"nursery--diaper-and-care-backstock","url":"/zones/nursery-the-diaper-and-care-backstock"},{"symptom":"There's no mat on the tub floor and no grab bar on the wall, and a guest is about to step in here well after dark","room":"Guest Bathroom","zone":"Shower or Tub","why":"A towel bar screwed into drywall isn't rated to take a person's weight, and nobody's added a proper anchor point","sixS":"Safety","action":"Take out every bottle and turn it over. This is where the household's rejected products retire: the shampoo nobody liked, the body wash that smells wrong, the conditioner welded to the shelf. Keep one shampoo, one conditioner, one body wash, all readable and more than a third full. The rest go, along with the old razor and the disintegrating loofah.","victory":"One shampoo, one conditioner and one body wash stand in the shower, each more than a third full and easy to read, with nothing else left welded to the shelf.","img":"guest-bathroom--shower-or-tub","url":"/zones/guest-bathroom-the-shower-or-tub"},{"symptom":"A solvent can and a water based paint can are sitting on the same shelf instead of separated","room":"Workshop","zone":"Finishing and Chemical Zone","why":"Incompatibles meeting on one shelf is the actual hazard this zone exists to prevent, and it outranks how tidy the shelf looks","sixS":"Safety","action":"Check every rag from today's finishing work: anything balled up loose goes into the lidded metal can with the lid pushed down, and scan the open cans on the shelf for one without a date and mark it now.","victory":"No oily rag is loose anywhere in the zone, and every open can on the shelf shows a marker date on its lid.","img":"workshop--finishing-and-chemical-zone","url":"/zones/workshop-the-finishing-and-chemical-zone"},{"symptom":"Flea and worming treatment sits loose in the open caddy at the same height as the waste bags a child is allowed to fetch","room":"Mudroom","zone":"Pet Station","why":"Poison stored at a height a child is encouraged to reach into for something else entirely is a safety constraint that outranks convenience","sixS":"Safety","action":"Clip the lead back on its hook right now and check the bag roll: if it's down to the last few, swap it for the spare. Check the food bin's level against the scoop and refill it if it has dropped that low, and move any treatment sitting loose in the caddy behind a closed door above reach.","victory":"The lead, collar and a full bag roll hang together as one kit on the hook, the food bin's level sits at or above the scoop line, and no treatment is loose in the open caddy.","img":"mudroom--pet-station","url":"/zones/mudroom-the-pet-station"},{"symptom":"The mirror or the biggest frame on the wall has some play in it when you push up and out on it","room":"Stair Landing","zone":"Wall and Display Zone","why":"I've never actually press-tested it, so I don't know how loose it's gotten","sixS":"Sort","action":"Walk the flight and take down every frame still hanging from a single nail or a sawtooth hanger, along with anything with cracked glass, and set them aside rather than rehanging them the same way.","victory":"No frame on the wall hangs from a single nail or a sawtooth hanger, and nothing with cracked glass has gone back up.","img":"stair-landing--wall-and-display-zone","url":"/zones/stair-landing-the-wall-and-display-zone"},{"symptom":"The umbrella stays cranked up overnight, or a household extension lead runs out to the string lights across boards that stay wet with dew","room":"Patio or Deck","zone":"Outdoor Dining Zone","why":"An open umbrella catching wind, or a lead lying in a puddle, is a real hazard, and that outranks the extra step of cranking it down or running proper outdoor-rated cord","sixS":"Safety","action":"Clear the table down to bare surface, crank the umbrella down, and tuck every chair fully under.","victory":"The table holds only the umbrella and the one weighted tray, the umbrella is cranked down, and every chair is tucked fully under.","img":"patio-or-deck--outdoor-dining-zone","url":"/zones/patio-or-deck-the-outdoor-dining-zone"}]};
